# Amazon Music API — Quick Reference

**Unofficial** wrapper around Amazon's internal / Music APIs. Hosted at:

```
https://amz.dezalty.com
```

Backend status is public; all catalog data is behind a JWT.

---

## Auth (required)

Every data endpoint requires:

```
Authorization: Bearer <session-token>
```

Without it → `401 {"detail":{"code":"missing_session_token", ...}}`.

A session token is a JWT minted from **your own Amazon account** via one of:

| Endpoint | Method | What you provide |
|---|---|---|
| `/auth/login` | POST | Amazon cookies as JSON/text (`ubid-main`, `at-main` retained; body `{"content": "...", "format": "auto", "expires_in": 86400}`) |
| `/auth/login/file` | POST | Upload a cookie file |
| `/auth/mobile/oauth-url` | GET | Generates Amazon Mobile OAuth PKCE registration URL |
| `/auth/mobile/exchange` | POST | Complete OAuth flow & issue JWT |
| `/auth/login/mobile` | POST | Existing `credentials_mobile.json` |

Token lifetime configurable 5 min – 30 days (default 1 day).

> Note: an even easier browser flow is advertised at `amz.dezalty.com/login`
> (star the GitHub repo to get tokens). The login page returns 404 on the API
> path directly — it's a web app, not a REST endpoint.

---

## Search

```
GET /search?query={query}&type={type}
```

`type` ∈ track, album, artist, playlist, ... Returns Amazon result items keyed by
**ASIN** (e.g. `B077F6QG2S`).

## Metadata endpoints (all by ASIN)

| Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|
| `GET /tracks/{asin}` | Track metadata (title, album, artist, release info) |
| `GET /albums/{asin}` | Album + track list |
| `GET /artists/{asin}` | Artist metadata + discography |
| `GET /playlists/{asin}` | Catalog playlist |
| `GET /playlists/{asin}/community` | Community playlist |
| `GET /podcasts/{asin}`, `GET /episodes` | Podcast content |
| `GET /tracks/{asin}/lyrics` | Lyrics |
| `GET /tracks/{asin}/streams` | Available DASH streams |
| `GET /tracks/{asin}/streams/{quality}` | Pick a stream by quality |

## Playback / DRM

- `POST /manifests/parse` — parse DASH manifest
- `POST /widevine/key` — acquire Widevine content key (PSSH → key)

Quality ladder: Low(48k OPUS) → Medium(192k) → Normal(320k) → High(≤16-bit
FLAC) → Master(24-bit ≤96kHz) → Max(24-bit ≤192kHz).

---

## Current status (tested 2026-09-16)

- `/health` → `{"status":true,"service":"amazon-music-api","version":"source"}`
- `/search` and `/session` → `401 missing_session_token` without a JWT.
- **Blocked:** the "Wyclef Jean / Young Thug" metadata lookup cannot run without
  a session JWT, and minting one requires real Amazon account cookies or mobile
  OAuth credentials.

**Conclusion:** like Qobuz, this API is account-gated. Provide Amazon session
cookies (or complete mobile OAuth) to get a Bearer token, then the search flow is:

```
POST /auth/login  -> JWT
GET /search?query=wyclef jean young thug&type=track  (Bearer)
GET /tracks/{asin}
GET /albums/{asin}
```